le_designation: null\n- description: \"An interruptible measuring system for liquids other than water.\"\n\nRecommendation:\n- id: \"R117\" (canonical, e.g. \"R60\"). R 117-1 (2007). Part 1. Hmm — \"R 117-1 (2007)\". The canonical id might be \"R117\". Edition: 2007? The edition is int. The recommendation is \"R 117-1 (2007)\" titled \"Dynamic measuring systems for liquids other than water\". Edition as int — 2007 is the year, not edition number exactly. For R117, editions are 1995, 2007... Actually the certificate number is \"R 117/2007-A-NL1-22.02\" so 2007 refers to edition year. I'll put edition: 2007? The schema says edition (int). Hmm. For R60 examples edition is 2000 (R60 (2000)). So edition: 2007. But it's \"R 117-1\" — part 1. Maybe id: \"R117-1\"? The canonical example says \"R60\" not \"OIML R 60\". I could use \"R117-1\" to preserve part. I think \"R117-1\" is more accurate. Hmm, but instruction says canonical id like \"R60\". R117 has parts 1, 2, 3. The certificate mentions \"R 117-1 (2007)\". I'll use id: \"R117-1\" with edition 2007. Alternatively id \"R117\". Let me think: the rule is canonicalization — strip \"OIML\" prefix. \"R 117-1\" → \"R117-1\". I'll go with \"R117-1\".\n- amendment: null (omit)\n- scheme: \"A\"\n- accuracy_classes: [0.3, 0.5, 1.0] — from \"0,3 / 0,5 / 1,0\". Convert commas to decimals: 0.3, 0.5, 1.0.\n\nTest reports:\n- No. NMi-2638810-01 dated 7 April 2022, 50 pages — this is the main type evaluation report? It says \"The conformity of the measuring system was established by the results of tests and examinations provided in the associated report(s): No. NMi-2638810-01...\" That's the type_evaluation_report.\n- Then many reports \"For the mechanical measurement transducer...\", \"measurement sensor...\", \"core processor...\", \"flow transmitter...\", \"electronic calculating and indicating device...\", \"gas extractor...\". These are reports for applicable parts — these would be test_reports with role... They're referenced conformity reports for components. The schema roles: type_evaluation_report | test_report | documentation_file | evaluation_report. These component reports could be role \"test_report\". Hmm, they're Type Evaluation/Approval certificates from earlier. I think role \"test_report\" is appropriate for the part reports.\n\nAlso documentation folder: \"The construction of the measuring instrument is recorded in the Documentation folder no. T12216-1.\" That could be test_reports entry with role \"documentation_file\": id \"T12216-1\".\n\nLet me list test reports:\n\nMain:\n1. NMi-2638810-01, 7 April 2022, 50 pages, role: type_evaluation_report\n\nMechanical measurement transducer (Silea Liquid Transfer S.r.l., type DM, BMxxx):\n2. NMi-19017928-01, 8 August 2018, 66 pages\n3. NMi-2273797-01, 5 April 2019, 27 pages\n\nMeasurement sensor (Emerson Process Management Flow B.V., type CMFxxxy, DS600):\n4. CVN-201269, 10 July 2002, 80 pages\n5. CVN-207999-01, 1 March 2003, 9 pages\n6. CVN-410178-1, 21 May 2005, 6 pages\n7. CVN-410178-2, 21 May 2005, 6 pages\n8. CVN-410178-3, 21 May 2005, 8 pages\n9. CVN-410178-4, 21 May 2005, 6 pages\n10. C-SP/603876, 19 December 2006, 23 pages\n11. CPC-607580-1, 26 April 2007, 93 pages\n12. CPC-802620-01, 17 December 2009, 41 pages\n13. NMi-10200543-2, 5 April 2011, 12 pages\n14. NMi-11200345-2, 20 November 2011, 10 pages\n15. NMi-1901179-01, 19 December 2017, 24 pages\n\nCore processor (Emerson, type 700, 800, 820, 1700, 2500, 2700, 3500, 3700 \"MVD series\"):\n16. CPC-307228-1, 21 February 2005, 35 pages\n17. CPC-607580-1, 26 April 2007, 32 pages (note: same number as above but different page count — 93 vs 32; the OCR lists it twice; keep both as listed, though it's probably an OCR artifact. Hmm. In the sensor list it says CPC-607580-1 93 pages; in core processor list CPC-607580-1 32 pages. I'll include both as given; don't fabricate.)\n18. CPC-610406-2, 29 January 2008, 142 pages\n19. CPC-710466-1, 19 November 2008, 64 pages\n20. NMi-11200214-0