SO13203381-01, NMi-SO13204037-01, NMi-SO14200881-01, NMi-1901208-01, NMi-1901208-02, NMi-1902436-01.\n4. flow transmitter: NMi-1902436-01, NMi-2571596-01, NMi-14200115-01..06, NMi-15200770-01.\n5. calculator Toptech Multiload II: CPC/705355, NMi-11200253, NMi-12200429, NMi-15200296-01, NMi-15200296-02, NMi-15200296-03.\n6. calculator Liquid Controls: NMi-2408986-01, NMi-2408986-02.\n7. gas extractor: CPC-9200487-01.\n\nAlternatives: the two calculating/indicating devices (Multiload II vs MASTERLOAD) — alternatives \"OR\"? The cert lists both brands as acceptable — arguably OR. And sensor types CMFxxxy vs DS600 — \"type CMFxxxy, DS600\" — that's a pattern for Coriolis sensors; CMFxxxy and DS600 are two type series. Ambiguous. I'll leave alternatives null except maybe between the two calculator entries — but alternatives is a field on a component entry, not between entries. So set null and not use it. Actually could set alternatives \"OR\" on... it's within one component. Skip; leave null/omit.\n\nType designations with wildcard: \"5700*1(2,3 or 5)A***ZZ*\" — keep exactly as in markdown: \"5700\\*1(2,3 or 5)A\\*\\*\\*ZZ\\*\". The escaped asterisks in markdown: `5700\\*1(2,3 or 5)A\\*\\*\\*ZZ\\*` — actual type is \"5700*1(2,3 or 5)A***ZZ*\". Use unescaped.\n\nNow viscosity: \"0,3 - 1242 mPa·s\" → min 0.3, max 1242, unit \"mPa·s\". unit_symbol: \"mPa·s\". Leave unit_id null.\n\nWrite final JSON. Keep it clean. Keys not present → omit.\n\nFor applicants and manufacturers — the layout \"Applicant and Manufacturer — Silea Liquid Transfer S.r.l.\" means the applicant is also the manufacturer. Include both arrays.\n\nDate_issued: \"2022-04-07\".\n\nCertificate number: include revision? Number field: \"R 117/2007-A-NL1-22.02\". Revision is separate (\"revision 0\"). Keep number without revision.\n\nFinal JSON:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R 117/2007-A-NL1-22.02\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"project_number\": \"2638810\",\n    \"page_total\": 15,\n    \"member_state\": \"The Netherlands\",\n    \"date_issued\": \"2022-04-07\",\n    \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"NMi Certin B.V.\",\n    \"address_lines\": [\"Thijsseweg 11\", \"2629 JA Delft\", \"The Netherlands\"],\n    \"person_responsible\": \"M.Ph.D. Schmidt\",\n    \"phone\": \"+31 88 636 2332\",\n    \"email\": \"certin@nmi.nl\",\n    \"website\": \"www.nmi.nl\",\n    \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\"\n  },\n  \"applicants\": [...],\n  \"manufacturers\": [...],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Measuring system\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"(Un)Loading, transferring, measuring system for depot, oil terminal, airport\"],\n    \"description\": \"An interruptible measuring system for liquids other than water. Each measuring instrument consists at least of: one pump, one measurement transducer (meter), one calculating/indicating device (calculator), optionally one gas elimination device (gas extractor).\"\n  },\n  \"components\": [...],\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"type_level\": {\n      \"intended_for_measurement\": {\"value\": \"Liquid other than water (excluding food liquids)\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": [\"*\"]},\n      \"viscosity_range\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 0.3, \"max\": 1242}, \"unit_symbol\": \"mPa·s\", \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": [\"*\"]}\n    }\n  },\n  \"recommendation\": {\n    \"id\": \"R117-1\",\n    \"edition\": 2007,\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"accuracy_classes\": [0.3, 0.5, 1.0]\n  },\n  \"test_reports\": [...],\n  \"revision_history\": [{\"revision\": \"0\", \"date\": \"2022-04-07\"}],\n  \"footnotes\": [{\"marker\": \"*\", \"text\": \"The actual characteristics are depending on the configuration and applicable parts chosen for the complete measuring system.\"}]\n}\n\nThe structured value shape: should I include unit_symbol: null and unit_id: null on string values? The schema example shows footnote_markers optional. Rule 2 says every value must be object with value, unit_symbol, unit_id, footnote_markers. I'll include all keys consistently.\n\nFor recommendation id: \"R117-1\" vs \"R117\". The example says e.g. \"R60\". I'll go with \"R117-1\" since the part matters for R117. Actually the certificate text: \"R 117-1 (2007)\". Canonical: \"R117-1\". Edition 2007. Good.\n\nAccuracy classes: 0.3, 0.5, 1.0 → [0.3, 0.5, 1.0] as numbers.\n\nNow test_reports array. Include duplicates? I'll dedupe exact duplicates (NMi-1902436-01 31 July 2018 27 pages appears twice → once). NMi-11200345-2 appears with two different dates → two entries. CPC-607580-1 two entries (93 and 32 pages). NMi-2571596-01 two entries (38 and 32 pages).\n\nFull list:\n\n1. {id: \"NMi-2638810-01\", date: \"2022-04-07\", pages: 50, role: \"type_evaluation_report\"}\n2. {id: \"NMi-19017928-01\", date: \"2018-08-08\", pages: 66, role: \"test_report\"}\n3. {id: \"NMi-2273797-01\", date: \"2019-04-05\", pages: 27, role: \"test_report\"}\n4. {id: \"CVN-201269\", date: \"2002-07-10\", pages: 80, role: \"test_report\"}\n5. {id: \"CVN-207999-01\", date: \"2003-03-01\", pages: 9, role: \"test_report\"}\n6. {id: \"CVN-410178-1\", date: \"2005-05-21\", pages: 6, role: \"test_report\"}\n7. {id: \"CVN-410178-2\", date: \"2005-05-21\", pages: 6, role: \"test_report\"}\n8. {id: \"CVN-410178-3\", date: \"2005-05-21\", pages: 8, role: \"test_report\"}\n9. {id: \"CVN-410178-4\", date: \"2005-05-21\", pages: 6, role: \"test_report\"}\n10. {id: \"C-SP/603876\", date: \"2006-12-19\", pages: 23, role: \"test_report\"}\n11. {id: \"CPC-607580-1\", date: \"2007-04-26\", pages: 93, role: \"test_report\"}\n12. {id: \"CPC-802620-01\", date: \"2009-12-17\", pages: 41, role: \"test_report\"}\n13. {id: \"NMi-10200543-2\", date: \"2011-04-05\", pages: 12, role: \"test_report\"}\n14. {id: \"NMi-11200345-2\", date: \"2011-11-20\", pages: 10, role: \"test_report\"}\n15. {id: \"NMi-1901179-01\", date: \"2017-12-19\", pages: 24, role: \"test_report\"}\n16. {id: \"CPC-3